proof.text:
For each $i<d-1$, both $A_i$ and $A_{i+1}$ vanish by Step 4, so the short exact sequence in Step 3 forces $B_i=0$. At $i=d-1$, the same sequence has a surjection $B_{d-1}	woheadrightarrow A_d
eq0$, so $B_{d-1}
eq0$ (including the boundary case $d=1$, where $B_0
eq0$). Rees [lem-weil-pbc-rees-ext-regular-sequence] for the nonzero finite module $Q$ and $I=\mathfrak m$ now gives a $Q$-regular sequence of length $d-1$ from the vanishing below $d-1$, and rules out a $Q$-regular sequence of length $d$ because $B_{d-1}
eq0$. Its finite depth $e$ is therefore $d-1$ by [def-weil-pbc-depth]. Hence $\operatorname{depth}(M/xM)=\operatorname{depth}(M)-1$.
